  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GIZ-Advancing Inclusive Just Energy Transition</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Africas transition to a low-carbon and climate-resilient economy presents both opportunities and challenges. While the government has taken significant steps, such as the Just Energy Transition Investment Plan (JET IP) and partnerships like the Just Energy Transition Partnership (JETP), a major challenge remains in ensuring that the workforce is adequately skilled to meet the demands of the renewable energy sector. The current Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET) system lacks specialized programs in renewable energy, limiting the employment prospects of young people. Additionally, high youth unemployment and the need for lecturer development further hinder the effectiveness of skills development initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
